From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:35:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: export dcache_inval_poc for diagnostics

The out-of-tree H713 HDMI diagnostic bridge reads a no-map DRAM ring written
by the capture engine.  A cacheable mapping needs an explicit invalidate to
observe those non-coherent writes, but arm64 does not currently export its
existing invalidate-to-PoC primitive to GPL modules.

Export the primitive so the diagnostic module can evaluate the cacheable read
path without duplicating architecture cache-maintenance assembly.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/mm/flush.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/mm/flush.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/mm/flush.c
@@ -85,6 +85,7 @@ void flush_dcache_page(struct page *page)
  * Additional functions defined in assembly.
  */
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(caches_clean_inval_pou);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(dcache_inval_poc);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_PMEM_API
 void arch_wb_cache_pmem(void *addr, size_t size)
